{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game","id":994549,"title":"Starting a Promethean Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T07:06:31-07:00","id":994549,"title":"Starting a Promethean Game","content":"Alright, so, there's interest on the forums for running a PbP Promethean game. The other two threads about this have already attracted a couple of players, so I'll get attention for that here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> , and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7372_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7372\" data-vbnamecard=\"7372\">Lady Gray</a> come on over here and start the official discussion!<br /> <br /> We've already gathered two Tammuz for this throng, what other Lineages should come into play? Did you guys have a specific setting in mind for this game? (If you don't, I've already got a few ideas that would be fun to explore). One of the themes of the game being proposed so far is Misunderstandings &amp; Misconceptions, what else do you guys want to see explored? The big thing for the Tammuz is introspection, language, and hard work- how do you want to see those incorporated?<br /> <br /> Are there any ideas or themes that are explicitly <i>off </i>the table?<br /> <br /> How long of a Pilgrimage are you guys expecting? Are we going for the four Refinement base requirement, or are we going for a ten Refinement epic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:42:00-07:00","id":994570,"title":"","content":"Well this is awesome. To be honest, I've never played Promethean before, but I've read and own all the books and I'm eager to give it a go. I was planning on making a pseudo-academic Frankenstein, someone who tries to understand the world by taking every experience she encounters apart and looking at it piece by piece, and in doing so may end up missing the point a lot of the time. So I think she could fit in with the theme of Misunderstandings and Misconceptions. I can also see introspection and to a lesser degree, language playing a part in that, with her trying to see how to fit herself into the pieces of humanity she's found, trying to cobble together a decent approximation. I think a theme I'd like to see explored to some degree or another is passion, and to what degree people shape their passions and are shaped by them, along with the idea that the reality of a situation will often end up taking a backseat to what people believe. I don't have any themes I'd want off the table specifically.<br /> <br /> As for length, I'm happy either way, but including some other Refinements beyond the base four would be my preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:05:04-07:00","id":994588,"title":"","content":"Passion, and people's beliefs, will definitely play a major aspect of the game- and that will, in turn, tie into the power of words. I can imagine Disquiet playing a rather serious influence on this theme, especially if it hits Stage 3 and up. Sounds like Cobalus and Phosphorum will be Refinements that one, or more, of the Throng will end up pursuing.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm leaning towards this particular Throng's journey being one that covers all ten Refinements, because that would be far, far too much fun, and it's a rare thing for a Promethean game to really get going and dive into the material.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a preference as to the setting, or further thoughts on their characters and their respective backstories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:39:33-07:00","id":994633,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Very curious to see what will happen =D<br /> Like Lady Gray, the pleasure of playing Promethean was something that had not been granted to me so far, but I own the books and am eager to play =D<br /> I'm fine with any length, really, but more than the basic four refinements would be very nice, I think, for the very reason you already mentioned.<br /> <br /> There might be some overlap with Caladriu's concept, which I'd be fine with but I'd not have a problem with creating another character if anyone feels there is too much overlap, either.<br /> My plan was a Tammuz focused on the physical, how bodies move and work and how you can change them - and how much they can take.<br /> <br /> Mark 5's Creator felt responsible enough to educate him a little and set him off on the path with a little knowledge on how to defend himself and even a name, but soon couldn't bear having to see how he puts somebody else through the same shit he had to endure, and departed. Mark 5 didn't take well to that, and should he meet his Creator is liable to communicate this non-verbally. He did, however, take his lessons to heart, for they gave him hope: Forging himself through dedication and exercise will give him a strong body. And with a strong body, he might also attain a strong soul (Refinement of Iron, basically).<br /> He is also fascinated by the appreciation for the stories of Vigilantes like Batman and Arrow: apparently, Warriors stepping in for those too weak to defeat themselves are liked/appreciated. And he wants to be liked so very, very much. That being physically stronger does not equal being the bully in a conflict is something he hasn't quite worked out yet.<br /> (hope this short overview is okay and the char is acceptable, if not, just tell me, will re-do/elaborate on the necessary parts)<br /> <br /> I think there is potential for both Misunderstandings/Misconceptions as well as hard work with that concept. I can also see introspection and passion figure into that (especially in combination with the formerly mentioned Misunderstandings and Hard Work). Language maybe not so much, but I've been proven wrong before, and the Power of Words sounds promising =D<br /> <br /> Something that would be off the table for me would be having to RP romantical and/or sexual scenes (I don't mind them taking place, just not having my Tammuz reciprocate them. That said, someone coming on to him is fine, as long as there's a way out for him, and might make for some fun awkward scenes^^).<br /> <br /> <br /> What did you have planned for the setting so far? Might provoke some braincells to come up with preferances, but so far, I have none^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:05:47-07:00","id":994649,"title":"","content":"Mark 5 sounds like an interesting character- definitely starting off on Ferrum. I'm not sure there'll be as much overlap as you think, since you're coming at a similar concept from different angles. Your character is an emulator of heroes who doesn't quite get the nuances of the role just yet, and it sounds like Caladriu's character is attempting to atone for past transgressions, so you've already got an interesting dynamic there.<br /> <br /> Just so we're perfectly clear, this is going to be a Promethean 2E game. So, would your first Role for Ferrum be Exemplar, Martyr, or Soldier? (Their philosophy seems Ferrum, but the narrative role you're proposing seems closer to a Stannum mindset. One of their Roles is Vigilante, after all). Also, out of curiosity, where did you character get their name? And what will their Bestowment be?<br /> <br /> Three of the settings in-book that I'd love to poke at are Prague, Portland, and/or Phoenix. Prague for... obvious reasons, given that two of our Prometheans are Tammuz, and Phoenix because it's close to Sedona, and Sedona is a freaking weird town where magical practitioners are so common the metaphysics shops can specialize. When I was last there, a bunch of people were going on pilgrimages out into the desert to experience vortices of energy that is supposed to be the life-giving substance of the universe, and I even saw a gentleman at a bar who was a professional Alchemist, and if that isn't Promethean as all get-out I don't know what is. Portland just because it's Portland, and the varied weird and wonderful parade of humanity in that city is gorgeous.<br /> <br /> However, if you're willing to trust me a little bit more as a Storyteller, I could run Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada. Coincidentally, this happens to be my hometown and where I live. It's also a weird city, with more authors per capita than almost anywhere else in North America, described of as being nearly as Gothic as Lovecraft's New England thanks to the literature and ghost tour scene here, and a massive landing pad for immigrant communities in Canada. We have the largest cultural festival in North America, and the second largest theatre festival. It also happens to house the Canadian Museum of Human Rights.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it's also a city I know intimately, and there's a lot more immersion I could pull out of my hat for that setting than for any of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:19:33-07:00","id":994653,"title":"","content":"Ah, 2e? Unfortunately I only have first edition books and I'm not in a position to get the second edition, so I guess that's me out. I hope you guys can find another player and I hope you enjoy yourselves. Unless of course you'd be willing to play first edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:56:10-07:00","id":994673,"title":"","content":"That's great to hear^^<br /> <br /> I'm torn between Martyr and Soldier here. I'd like to give that some more thought. And while I agree that it is similar to Stannum to an extent, for Mark 5 being a Vigilante is not about wrath or vengeance or even Punishment, it's more about combining the practical (improving his ability) with the wonderful (people like batman, if I am batman, they will like me, too!) I feel like this approach leaves a lot of paths to potential Refinements open: Stannum, if he turns bitter, Aurum, if the fascination of and desire for human attention gets into his focus, Aes if he learns and aspires to one of the lessons superheros teach (putting other's needs above yours, that is), and Cobalus if he is ponders the failings of the humans around him - and his own. And in addition anything that might come up through the story, so I think there is maleability there.<br /> The Character was named by his creator, but whether his creator already attempted to create Progeny four times or whether he simply took the name of one of the things on the abandoned military site Mark 5 considers his birthplace, he does not know (neither do I, I'd leave that open to you, whatever makes for a more fun story^^).<br /> Heart of Clay looks awesome, so if that's fine with you, I'd pick that one up !<br /> <br /> So many different cities, sounds great! =D However, the Winnipeg approach got my curiousity, too. You got me at &quot;nearly as Gothic as Lovecraft&quot; and the fact that you live there is obviously very intriguing for a setting. Hm. Maybe exchange Portland and Phoenix for Winnipeg? Let's see what the others have to say =)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:23:26-07:00","id":994708,"title":"","content":"Conveniently, there's a massive deserted military base in the core of one of Winnipeg's neighbourhoods. There's a lot of debate about what to do with it. The federal government doesn't want to give it up, and the local (very large) First Nations population wants it for an urban reserve. Considering it's on Treaty Land, they've got an excellent claim to it, but I doubt there'll be much progress in the near future. It's also right beside a decent-sized abandoned high school, which would be a neat hideout for people.<br /> <br /> For an idea of what Gothic Winnipeg is like, here's a Tumblr post: <a href=\"http://queenbeyondthewalll.tumblr.com/post/115997182313\" target=\"_blank\">http://queenbeyondthewalll.tumblr.com/post/115997182313</a><br /> <br /> Oh, and then there's <i>these </i>lovely quotes: <i>Since there is horror here, and since the horror cannot be stopped, since hope is gone and the world is a nightmare of chaos, we must be in Winnipeg.</i><br /> \u2013Jonathan Ball, Preface to The Shadow Over Portage and Main<br /> <br /> <i>Winnipeg the ruin, Winnipeg of the haunted past, Winnipeg of</i><br /> <i>murder and flames. Winnipeg of cold and death, Winnipeg of the</i><br /> <i>hopeless, Winnipeg the doomed. </i><br /> \u2013Jonathan Ball, Preface to The Shadow Over Portage and Main<br /> <br /> ^ Said Dr. Jonathan Ball was my Year 1 English prof. He was awesome. And yeah, the whole anthology is named after a Lovecraft story. There's also some lovely horror comics written by a guy Dr. Ball brought to lecture at one of our classes, GMB Chomichuk. This is a link to his graphic novel Underworld: <a href=\"http://www.renegadeartsentertainment.com/underworld\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.renegadeartsentertainment.com/underworld</a><br /> <br /> You see the building the corpse giant is standing beside? I work in it. His website is called <i>Comic Alchemy</i>. The SyFy show <i>Channel Zero</i>? It was filmed here. I know I'm selling it really hard, but I'm starting to really get behind the idea of my home city in the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 10-28-2016, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:50:07-07:00","id":994722,"title":"","content":"Just FYI while we're sharing: I've run Promethean for my home group before, but only for a couple sessions. I've also briefly played 1E Promethean characters in mixed groups, and I'm currently a player in a 2E Promethean chronicle. I've read the 1E books front to back, I love their writing.<br /> <br /> I'm open to planning a ten-refinement pilgrimage, I'm just very skeptical by nature of assuming that any game (especially PBP) will go on a long time. My ideal Promethean chronicle as a player would be one that jumps around in space and time (narratively, not supernaturally), where each Chapter is like an important week in the characters' lives, and they don't immediately follow each other. Lots of timeskips and multiple locations, returning to some of the major ones later. Zooming in on the most exciting moments and Milestones and letting them play out how they will, with the understanding that there's (potentially) prolonged downtime between chapters where the characters go in and out of each others' lives. Some of the Promethean fiction has this assumption where the throng isn't together all the time, and they reconvene to travel as a full group only every few months or so. That would be cool!<br /> <br /> I'll quote something I said while planning a different game that didn't get off the ground:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it doesn't need to be a big epic chronicle in terms of length (although high personal stakes are great), I'm just looking for something to check in on and enjoy semi-casually. I like jumping right into &quot;the most interesting day in the character's life,&quot; in storytelling terms, not so much the slow long-term buildup that's not as well-suited to play-by-post in my experience.<br /> <br /> General idea for Promethean: maybe my favorite thing about the Frankenstein story is the relationship between creator and created, the weird ugly family bond these two have, the idea that Frankenstein can't just &quot;get rid of&quot; the Creature now that he's out in the world, even if he dearly wants to. I think a cool focus or building block for a game would be a very stormy relationship between two Prometheans, one created by the other, or maybe two Prometheans who share a creator. Maybe I could play a more experienced character trying to track down my wayward progeny to fulfill a major milestone, or vice versa, looking for my creator and trying to bury the hatchet. Or a small throng of two estranged &quot;siblings&quot; looking for their mutual creator, a good twin and a bad twin of sorts. </div> </div> </div>So the way that Prometheans (and other creatures) create others for various reasons and have various relationships with their progeny and creator is really interesting to me and something I'd like to highlight. There's an RPG I love called Progenitor, where it's a superhero setting with contagious powers- using your powers on someone might cause them to gain powers of their own, like how Generation works in oWoD Vampire. The big idea is that supers have a way of creating their own enemies, like how Batman kind of causes his rogues' gallery to exist. That would be really fun to play with, like the connections between a lineage of Prometheans, or more broadly the way that using powers or causing Disquiet/Wasteland has unintended consequences that are also deeply personal.<br /> <br /> For setting: again, I'd like to jump around a little, but Winnipeg sounds very cool, especially being in a city with lots of immigrants and refugees. I'm imagining my character being made in Arizona or somewhere in the Southwest, so a homecoming in Phoenix/Sedona would be fun. Prague would also be fun for the Golem connection and a Euro setting- I pretty much like all of the settings in the core book, honestly, although the lightning strikes and rogue alchemists of Johannesburg is maybe my favorite and it would be fun to have a Chapter or two there. The one thing I'd add is that I'd really enjoy some wilderness adventure, going out to the deep snowy forest in northern Canada for example. I know Going to the Wastes isn't a strong thing anymore in 2E, but dealing with some truly wild supernatural weirdness miles away from any human settlement would be really fun.<br /> <br /> Some things I like in general: high strangeness, qashmallim and Firestorms, and weird supernatural things that don't fit into any neat World of Darkness category. There's a great story in the Firestorm Chronicle Anthology that pits a Zeka against some Valravens, supernatural crows that prey on humans with royal blood because...that's apparently a thing that exists. It would also be fun to get glimpses of the formal supernatural societies of the larger setting, meeting up with a rogue Ordo Dracul scholar or a camp of Predator Kings in the deep wilderness. I'm interested in doing Argentum at some point if you couldn't tell.<br /> <br /> If you're open to it, I'd prefer if we could start with a little more XP than a starting character, and assume that we're familiar with the basics of the Pilgrimage. Suggestion: we could declare one Role that we've already completed, and get 10 Experiences to spend out of the gate, divided between regular Experiences and Vitriol. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:08:56-07:00","id":994734,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the time skips, and I agree that it <i>absolutely </i>makes sense given the fluff of Promethean. High Weirdness is always a lot of fun, and I'm a huge fan of <i>qashmallim </i>and Firestorms and just about everything else out there. They will absolutely play a part in this game. I'm also totally open to the idea of declaring one Role complete and giving you 10 Experiences to divide between regular Experiences and Vitriol as you see fit. That would still put you on your first Refinement, but definitely having made steps.<br /> <br /> The theme of Lineage seems to make a lot of sense, especially seeing as you two are playing Tammuz (and I have a personal soft spot for the Lineage as well).<br /> <br /> Chapters (and, to a lesser extent, Stories) being important flashpoints in a Pilgrimage makes a lot of sense to me, and I could definitely see some globe-trotting going on, as you do in a story about wandering, lonely, 'artificial' beings. Jumping between Winnipeg, the far north, Phoenix/Sedona, and Prague makes sense to me (I'll have to think of how to make Johannesburg work, but I'm sure I can come up with <i>something</i>.) and you guys will definitely be getting crossover elements.<br /> <br /> Another fun little detail of Winnipeg is that there's a relatively well-known goth club known as Elysium. No points for guessing what <i>that </i>translates to in CofD terms.<br /> <br /> Oh, and here's a post from Dr. Ball's blog with the Preface he wrote for The Shadow Over Portage and Main explaining the idea of 'Winnipeg Gothic' : <a href=\"http://www.jonathanball.com/winnipeg-horror-the-shadow-over-portage-and-main/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jonathanball.com/winnipeg...tage-and-main/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:06:18-07:00","id":994772,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7372_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7372\" data-vbnamecard=\"7372\">Lady Gray</a> &gt; That's too damn bad =( I wouldn't mind playing either, really.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a><br /> <br /> I didn't know anything about Winnipeg prior to this, really, but the city is growing on me already xD<br /> <br /> The scope and thematic range look awesome to me. Totally down with this. Regarding the timeskips: what range of time are we talking? Cause I don't have Dark Eras (yet!).<br /> <br /> One more thing we might want to consider: posting times/frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:03:43-07:00","id":994815,"title":"","content":"Thanks for linking the blog, this is actually really interesting stuff. Especially because I know nothing about Winnipeg!<br /> <br /> Here's what I had in mind for my character. I want something kind of like the sample character Chicago from the 2E book, turning to Flux as a failure state and eventually climbing out of it.<br /> <br /> Earth Crisis was created in a shallow grave outside of Phoenix for the purpose of fulfilling a milestone for her lonely creator. Creating her wasn't enough, she had to teach her to master Ferrum as she had. But she didn't have the temperament for it, her body was too scrawny, she resented being created for someone else's checklist, and so she was a disappointment to her. They fought, a lot, with words and then with fists and lightning, and eventually parted ways. She went from Ferrum to Stannum, and eventually in fury and despair stepped off the Pilgrimage and became Hundred-Handed. She stopped going by Earth Crisis, and eventually became known as Earth-Dies-Screaming in the Rambles of others. Since she couldn't become strong in the way her creator wanted, she spat in her face by embracing Flux and mutating her body into all sorts of wonderful and horrible forms.<br /> <br /> When she was roaming, she met someone else who had abandoned her Pilgrimage, a Galateid called Dead Girl. They were strongly attracted to each other, but being in Flux, it mutated into something corrosive and damaging. Dead Girl coerced her into joining a branded throng with her, and with a pack of Pandorans at their side, the two of them did awful things to each other and the world for more than two years. They harrowed her creator more than once, and other Prometheans too, and became infamous. It ended when the two of them were separated in a Firestorm that killed their Pandorans. The pain from the fire somehow cleared away the cobwebs. She'd always felt a strange attraction to fire.<br /> <br /> Slowly, steadily, she crawled back onto the Pilgrimage. She just goes by Earth now, but they still tell stories about her. She's back in Stannum, but at least she's trying to learn something from her fury now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:48:59-07:00","id":994977,"title":"","content":"Earth sounds like a fascinating character to play. Here's the important question though- do you see Dead Girl as having survived the Firestorm and/or returned to the Pilgrimage? And, if we're doing flashbacks (and/or flash forwards) would you want to explore Earth's days as Earth-Dies-Screaming?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, what was Dead Girl like? Beyond being Earth's girlfriend and a Centimanus Galateid? Also, how did Mark 5 and Earth meet?<br /> <br /> Beyond that, let's get into the details of character creation now. What are their Aspirations? And what are the answers to the Five Questions?<br /> <br /> <b>What Sort of Human Do You Want to Be?<br /> <br /> How Have Humans Taught You To Fear and Hate?<br /> <br /> How Did You Split With Your Creator?<br /> <br /> What Keeps You on the Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> What Would You Give Up to Become Human?</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:03:45-07:00","id":995001,"title":"","content":"Survived the Firestorm yes, returned to the Pilgrimage...possibly/unknown? Maybe she isn't a monster anymore either, but misses the strange freedom of giving up completely and the power they had over Flux in a horrible way and wants to go back, but she's scared to do it alone. If you're familiar with the show Steven Universe at all, I was imagining them being similar to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IuYwQI9keJ4\" target=\"_blank\">Lapis Lazuli and Jasper</a>. I like the idea of two characters who had a supernatural bond that's also heavily coded as a mundanely abusive and unhealthy relationship, and the PC trying to move forward while the other party is still out there in the world somewhere, hoping to draw them back in because they're just that broken. Dead Girl could be a looming antagonist that's extremely personal in a way that most villains aren't, and a concrete way of Earth's past actions endangering the throng.<br /> <br /> Dead Girl used to practice Aurum and Plumbum and Aes, which created their branded throng and made their bond tight and powerful. If she's returned to the Pilgrimage, she probably practices Cobalus now. She was precise and controlling and intelligent and strangely elegant, while Earth was the harsh and tough and direct one. She was created as a 30something white woman intended to look more sweet and pleasant and adorable than traditionally beautiful. When she realized what most people were actually seeing in her and in human women, she was confused, then afraid, then disgusted, and increasingly grew to hate them for their ignorance and cruelty to each other. She had a throng once, and a desire to make her body her own instead of an object for others or a vehicle for the Pilgrimage, but that was a long time ago, and Flux has a way of twisting even the most noble justifications for embracing it until nothing is left but dissolution and madness.<br /> <br /> As for flashbacks: that's a storytelling technique I like and it would definitely be fun to play a Centimanus PC for the occasional scene in a story, just to revel in some weirdness and body horror. Maybe a brief flashback if something is relevant or the throng encounters something she would know about or have some connection to. I mostly want it as &quot;awful period that happened in the past,&quot; but I'd be up for rolling some dice there.<br /> <br /> Considering what Mark 5 is into, maybe Earth is practicing the Vigilante role of Stannum when they meet. They could have been drawn together by both feeling the powerful Azothic Radiance of some Firestorm or qashmal or whatever, and once they found each other, they talked and compared notes and found that they're kind of doing the same thing and decided to team up for a while. One's a Golem, the other one's also a Golem, but different. Together, They Fight Crime!<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> edit: random thoughts about Tammuz themes. Introspection is an easy one, thinking and reflecting on her progress and trouble so far and the different struggles of others, trying to be empathetic for others. Hard work in the sense that Earth doesn't really have much hope that she'll be able to complete the Pilgrimage at all after what she's done, and because she's prone to get really melancholic and down on herself and stop trying when she fails at anything, but she's stubborn enough to keep at it. For language, I was thinking it would be an interesting image if her body had some sort of speech impediment, and her lingering Flux scars only exacerbated it. It's like a metaphor or something!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-28-2016, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:09:52-07:00","id":995060,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I like the idea of Dead Girl sort of just... hanging around. Somewhere out there. Looming like a dark cloud over Earth's Pilgrimage. Maybe she'll reach out, maybe she'll try and reconnect, maybe she'll try and turn Earth back to the Refinement of Flux... or maybe she just wants closure. I like the idea of Schrodinger's Dead Girl until that aspect of the story must be confronted directly. I also imagine that, if those two were as formidable a pair of Centimanni as you suggest, certain notable <i>sublimati </i>might be aware of them, but I'll probably save that for when we leave Canada.<br /> <br /> Here's a thing a just thought of- you chose the Inscribed Bestowment for Earth, yeah? What is the inscription? Where is it? What does it say? Does it have any particular significance to Earth? Does she, as the new Tammuz splat page implies, remember something of what she was before she was a Promethean? Perhaps, when she forgives herself, she'll get past her difficulties with language, and attain the mastery of it that the more academically-inclined Golems are said to possess.<br /> <br /> More pointedly, what's the craft that Earth drives herself towards? All Tammuz have that <i>one thing </i>which becomes their obsession, the thing they work hard at, which becomes the thing they work well at. Examples in the splat section include construction &gt; architecture, wood carving, protecting the Throng, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:15:24-07:00","id":995114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=994977#post994977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how did Mark 5 and Earth meet?<br /> <br /> Beyond that, let's get into the details of character creation now. What are their Aspirations? And what are the answers to the Five Questions?<br /> <br /> <b>What Sort of Human Do You Want to Be?<br /> <br /> How Have Humans Taught You To Fear and Hate?<br /> <br /> How Did You Split With Your Creator?<br /> <br /> What Keeps You on the Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> What Would You Give Up to Become Human?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Mark 5 and Earth meeting up peacefully like Caladriu described, but I could also see Mark 5 hearing about Earth-Dies-Screaming from someone else's Ramble and taking it upon him to take out the dangerous Centimanus, only to meet a kind of (redeemed?in-the-process-of-redemption?) kindred spirit instead.<br /> <br /> Aspirations:<br /> Save someone's life <i>and </i>receive gratitude for it.<br /> Teach someone to defend himself.<br /> (not sure about long-term yet, but Defending someone's Milestone sounds nice, even though I wouldn't know how that'd look in practice xD)<br /> Edit: if there is some sort of danger/foe present, be it supernatural or mortal, I'd switch teaching someone to defend himself for dealing with that.<br /> Long-term Aspiration of becoming a True Hero, maybe?<br /> <br /> For the Five Questions I got this:<br /> <br /> What Sort of Human do you want to be? Someone who's liked, even looked up to.<br /> How have Humans taught you to fear and hate? By driving me away and even attacking me when all I do is help them.<br /> How did you split with your creator? Was suddenly left alone, without a word. Despite all the help before the departure, that left a bitter taste.<br /> What keeps you on the Pilgrimage? Loneliness and dedication.<br /> What would you give up to become Human? My Name.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, the possibilty to have fulfilled one role would mean Mark 5 is a Soldier now, having been a Martyr beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 10-29-2016, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:26:19-07:00","id":995318,"title":"","content":"Alright, Mark 5 is starting to shape up. That certainly makes sense in terms of the two meeting up. I don't imagine the game will start with a set antagonist- I'll let you guys dig yourselves into trouble instead of starting with an obstacle in your path. Aspirations are looking good. Would Mark 5 want to meet their genitor again?<br /> <br /> What was the lesson Mark learned from being a Martyr? Vitriol (and Milestones) are distilled enlightenment after all. What are your Alembics? You'll have two each in Vitality and Corporeum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:01:06-07:00","id":995334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=995114#post995114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Mark 5 and Earth meeting up peacefully like Caladriu described, but I could also see Mark 5 hearing about Earth-Dies-Screaming from someone else's Ramble and taking it upon him to take out the dangerous Centimanus, only to meet a kind of (redeemed?in-the-process-of-redemption?) kindred spirit instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea is way better, let's do that instead!<br /> <br /> Earth's Inscription is a tattoo wrapped around her bicep which reads &quot;A MAN OF WORDS AND NOT OF DEEDS IS LIKE A GARDEN FULL OF WEEDS.&quot; She knows that this phrase was important to her creator, but doesn't know its origin. As her creator explained it, it means that she was built to work and not to speak, the idea being that a garden full of weeds is a bad thing to be. After everything she's been through so far, she's decided she doesn't want to read the tattoo as a constant reminder of her failure, and instead interprets it backwards. Words are a valuable kind of deed, and a weed-choked garden could also be called a place teeming with life, even if it's not the life the gardener expected. It currently gives bonuses to Expression, Intimidate, and Survival.<br /> <br /> Related: her creator intended for her to fight and grow physically strong as her purpose, but after so much failure and disappointment, Earth doesn't really want that. She <i>does </i>have an affinity for gardening, raising animals (or Pandorans at least), and generally working in the dirt and training and cultivating and being responsible for other life.<br /> <br /> She remembers a time before she broke out of the Arizona desert, but doesn't have words to describe it. The general sense of it is a creator greater than the one who physically made her. She believes this space or time or creator or feeling is what she glimpses in her Vivid Dreams sometimes.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>What sort of human do you want to be?</b><br /> &quot;Handsome, masculine, tall, I guess. Mostly I don't wanna need people to like me or care whether they respect me or not, because I'm so sure of who I am and where I'm supposed to be that I've got everything I need already. I want there to be no one I'd rather be than me.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>How have humans taught you to fear and hate?</b><br /> &quot;I ain't afraid of humans, they're afraid of me. What would I be afraid of? Anyone who tries to fuck with me is gonna end up dead.<br /> <br /> I hate humans because they're beautiful to me. It's not even anger, they're just...there, in my brain, dancing and laughing and holding hands and shit. Not laughing at me, they don't care about me, I know that. Just being happy being themselves. Even when I was a Freak, they were still in my head, still beautiful. That's what got me out.<br /> <br /> I think the Principle created humans to show me what I can't have. What I can never have.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>How did you split with your creator?</b><br /> &quot;Heartsblood was this big scary Tammuz, 7 foot tall, hard as granite with a big leather apron and an Azothic sledgehammer, and she lurched around the Southwest looking for stuff strong enough to fight. Eventually she made me. She needed me to become strong enough to beat her in a fair fight, but I came out wrong, and I was never good enough- and that doesn't feel right, being shit at the one thing you were made for. I kept trying to leave and do my own thing, but she brought me back, usually because I was gonna get myself killed by Disquiet.<br /> <br /> Eventually she figured she should just kill me and try again, and that was the <i>real</i> Milestone. Like I was just a bump in her road. I didn't like that. I fell into Stannum, and <i>now </i>I could put up a good fight, on my terms. Don't need to be tough to throw lightning bolts. We fought a lot, I'd run for a few days and she'd catch me and we'd fight again, or I'd find her 'cause I wasn't done being angry yet. But eventually I limped away from a fight that wrecked her Hovel, and she didn't catch me.<br /> <br /> That wasn't the end though. When I was a Freak, me and Dead Girl tracked her down again, more than once. Like, even when <i>she</i> started trying to run away from <i>me</i>, get a new throng, learn from some humans- we would find them and break them, because we liked hurting her. It was bad.<br /> <br /> Finally we had this big ugly throwdown at the Grand Canyon during a thunderstorm last summer, Heartsblood versus me and Dead Girl and our pack. It went on for days, because we kept getting recharged. Finally she took a tumble, and we walked away alive. That one made it into the Ramble: 'The Battle of the Canyon,' they call it. I heard that story a few weeks back, sound effects and all, and realized we were the bad guys. Makes me wonder who they heard the story from.<br /> <br /> That's the last time I saw my creator. So far, anyway. I'd be surprised if a fall killed a Ferrum that tough.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>What keeps you on the Pilgrimage?</b><br /> &quot;Not hope, really. Hope is a mistake.<br /> <br /> More like knowing the alternative. I've been off the road, and it fucking sucked. You imagine there's a point where things get so bad that they break and you magically push through into something different and better, but that point doesn't exist. You just keep being a monster. It never ends.<br /> <br /> Gotta keep pushing this stupid boulder, no matter how many times it rolls back down the hill. Sisyphus is in Hell, but at least he has a purpose.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>What would you give up to become human?</b><br /> &quot;My memories. My footprint. My past. Heartsblood. Dead Girl. All of it, the good and the bad. I don't want the stories other monsters tell about me, or the nightmares, or the memories of what I've done and stolen and killed. I want none of this to have ever happened, and I want a blank slate.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's cowardly. But I know I'm not strong enough to face the wreckage. The people I left behind have to sift meaning out of what I did, and I can't help them with that. I can't make this better. The most I can do is run away and hope if I become human, I'll never have existed at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Aspirations:<ul><li>Throw down some lightning in combat.</li> <li>Meet someone who knows her through Repute.</li> <li>Learn what's become of Dead Girl. (Long-term)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:05:40-07:00","id":995369,"title":"","content":"I'll put in &quot;Subdue a Villain&quot; as Aspiration then. We'll see who the villain is together =D<br /> <br /> Meeting the genitor, yes. He'd like to punch his face in for leaving him behind without letting him know why. He'd also like to listen to the why. He'd also like to thank him for the gift he was given, the training and everything; he knows that's not exactly a standard. The fact that life is wonderful and he has such a huge chance, and the fact that it's awful and he has to suffer so much, he'd like to talk about that, too. Preferably with as few words as possible. So it'd be an... interesting meeting, I think ^^<br /> <br /> Hard work pays off. The body, human or Promethean, is capable of incredible feats, but those are only possible with hard work. The world is sublime, threatening at times, but the so-called fragile humans survive floods, earthquakes, wild fires and more. Even more, they jump from buildings, climb without safety, dive without equipment, all things incredibly dangerous. Why do they invest the time and energy to learn survival techniques or climb mountains in this day and age though? Because they want to show off. They want to show that they are indomitable, stronger than the world around them. Just like Prometheans, humans didn't get to chose what they'd start life with - but they can chose what they make out of themselves. &quot;I build myself. What you are is who you build step by step through your actions and decisions.&quot;<br /> Is that acceptable as a lesson for Maryr? atm I'm tired and have no idea how to put it into a short sentence ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> Alembics would be Corporeum: Hygeius, Corporeum: Motus, Vitality: Unbowed and Vitality: Unbroken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:25:25-07:00","id":995378,"title":"","content":"Hey, is it to late to join in the PbP game? I've got little to no experience with the PbP system, but am a huge Promethean 2E fan and have always wanted to be a player in a Created Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T19:31:27-07:00","id":995478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=995334#post995334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snipped for brevity</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all amazing. Any thoughts as to what the Role in Stannum you completed was, what you learned from it, and what Alembics you have now? (I'm assuming Arc is one of them, and I can't imagine Weaponize being unlikely either) I think having Heartsblood as another looming threat in the background. There are definitely serious skeletons in Earth's closet that need to be explored.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> that all works very well. That is certainly a suitable lesson from Martyr- Milestones are all about what <i>you </i>learn from the experience, especially Roles. It's all about the personal interpretation, about discovering yourself.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> it is most certainly not too late! Go right ahead and submit a character concept- I'm more than happy to get the chance to be a Storyteller; the more Prometheans the merrier. Or, well, the more eventually miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:19:09-07:00","id":995499,"title":"","content":"Look at all these named NPCs and plot hooks I'm giving you!<br /> <br /> Yeah, Arc and Weaponize for sure, and also Imperatus and Redirect.<br /> <br /> There was a moment when she consciously decided to come back to the Pilgrimage, but the actual transition was very gradual. She became a Savage, a Role she had attempted before leaving the path, but hadn't really understood before. She was still stalking prey and lurking in the wilderness and breaking shit and driving fear into human hearts, but now she stayed far away from Pandorans and no longer warped her flesh or invoked Flux.<br /> <br /> Recently she blew into a real small town in Manitoba called Powerview-Pine Falls, maybe a thousand people, used to be a papermill town until the mill shut down after the Great Recession. It reminded her of something she'd seen with Dead Girl, a dying lumber town in Oregon where the ghost of the foreclosed mill was demanding human sacrifices from the people too poor or stubborn to move on. The memories brought her rage. So she busted into the old mill, caused a stir, beat down some Disquieted squatters, broke a bunch of equipment, burned a bunch of Pyros, and within a few days turned the whole building into a Wasteland. Eventually she climbed up to the roof like King Kong and rained lightning down on the mill and surrounding buildings, expecting to revel in the screams.<br /> <br /> The thing that stuck in her mind was looking down from her perch and seeing a cop staring back up at her from the small crowd below. There was a woman with him. He had a gun, but he wasn't pointing it at her, he was just holding the woman painfully tight.<br /> <br /> Earth thought: <i>This hurts you. What I'm doing is hurting you. You are going to remember this.</i><br /> <br /> Earth-Dies-Screaming had done this routine many times before, but now Earth was looking at it through the eyes of the humans, and grasping the idea that she had now become <i>a thing that happened to this community, </i>something they would pull together or break apart over, just like the papermill shutting down.<br /> <br /> She climbed down from the roof and moved on. That was just a few weeks ago, the papermill Wasteland is probably still there.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Just realized that since completing a Role is a superlative Milestone, do we start at Pilgrimage 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:32:56-07:00","id":995504,"title":"","content":"Completing a Role <i>may </i>be a superlative Milestone, but given it's your first Role, I can definitely see it as one, so yes, you guys will all start with Pilgrimage 2. Out of curiosity, what, exactly, was the Role that Earth completed in doing so? I'm assuming it was the Savage, and now you've moved onto the Vigilante?<br /> <br /> How does Earth see herself now? Obviously, she still sees herself as a monster, but now she's a monster with a purpose. What's her take on the Vigilante so far?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, as a note to all players, I would draw up your characters on the Dalines sheet generator/dice roller, since it's explicitly a nWoD/CofD based website.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>, who do your characters think of the Divine Fire? What do they believe about the Principle or the <i>qashmallim</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 10-30-2016, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T23:52:03-07:00","id":995532,"title":"","content":"Sweet, glad to hear there's room. Love the ideas currently going around too, will do my best to help out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Trying to flesh out a character idea right now, leaning towards either a good old Frankenstein or one of the Unfleshed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:40:49-07:00","id":995542,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> You're preying on my weakness for writing long character development posts :/<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> Very cool, I was hoping we'd get more players! Either of those would be good IMO.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> She completed Savage, now she's Vigilante.<br /> <br /> If Earth stops working to think about <i>herself </i>in depth, it's melancholy-infused variations on &quot;you're not fooling anyone, you're worthless without Dead Girl, what's the point of looking for something you can't have, you never had a chance, two wrongs don't make a right, you're just one big super-wrong,&quot; etc etc. So instead, she usually locks up all those thoughts in Pandora's Box and focuses on the present!<br /> <br /> The Vigilante is kinda like that familiar story in the Azothic Memory about the people that put all their sins inside of a scapegoat and run the goat outside the village walls. They drive it out, but they also need it. The Vigilante is outside the community, but they also regulate it, they're not completely separate. The Vigilante does the things that people want to happen, but are afraid to do themselves. So she helps them. This is how she displays her heroism.<br /> <br /> Her usual MO so far is to hang around people whom the neighborhood fears and despises, then use Disquietism to build up her own Disquiet and focus it on the people who need to be punished. She helps the community fulfill their longing by turning their hatred of her onto the people they're afraid to act against.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Earth's Elpis is <b>Faith: </b>not necessarily human religious belief, not necessarily benevolent or malignant, although it can be any of these. It's the uniquely human attitude that despite all evidence to the contrary, there is something greater at play, some unseeable hope that will carry the day. Standing against the mundane world with the power of the irrational. Challenging someone to a fight that you have no chance of winning, refusing to follow human laws because you serve a non-empirical higher power, finding meaning in a senseless tragedy. Somewhere between Hope and Courage and Drive and simple stubbornness. Incidentally, in her time in Canada she's become very interested in Louis Riel for this reason, and wants to learn whether the Divine Fire inspired his rebellion somehow. [for the record, her Torment is <b>Alienated</b>]<br /> <br /> With that in mind: for her, the Principle is the desperate hope that's too fragile to mention out loud. She knows that Dead Girl would laugh if she heard her say it, but she badly wants to believe that there's a greater meaning behind all of this, that somewhere in the heart of the Divine Fire there's a Principle that knows her by name and says &quot;yes, spark of my flame, you are seen and you are exactly where you are expected to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> When she's closer to Torment, the Principle becomes the cruel animating force of the cosmos, the architect of all her suffering, mocking her with the impossible hope that she could ever turn lead into gold. The victories of other Prometheans are engineered to prove just how hopeless she really is.<br /> <br /> Earth-Dies-Screaming had a Vivid Dream about the <i>qashmallim </i>once, after that last Firestorm shook her out of her complacency. She still remembers it. She was laying broken at the bottom of the Grand Canyon in the dead of night, twisted and mutated and afraid, and she cried out and begged for help until finally <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/IJknuy0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">an angel in the shape of a swarm of butterflies</a> floated down and alighted on her.<br /> <br /> She said: &quot;I am in pain.&quot; The angel said: &quot;I know.&quot;<br /> <br /> She said: &quot;Will you make it stop?&quot; The angel said: &quot;No. But we are in pain with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> She wept. The angel waited.<br /> <br /> She said: &quot;Will the pain ever end?&quot; The angel said: &quot;Yes. One day, the pain will end.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's about as useful as the <i>qashmallim </i>usually are for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:08:15-07:00","id":995689,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> A Frankenstein would be an interesting way to, eventually, incorporate Johannesburg into the story. One the other hand, the Unfleshed are <i>always </i>a fascinating character archetype.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Character development is great for everyone! It gives you a better idea of Earth, it gives everyone a better idea of how to interact with her, and it gives <i>me </i>fuel for future stories, and ideas on how to flesh out the world. The Principle is probably one of my favourite cosmic forces in the CofD, so it will definitely come into play in a big way. Also, <i>qashmallim </i>are really fun to run considering they're so bizarre compared to other Ephemeral Beings.<br /> <br /> I'm going to enjoy mixing Anthropology, Philosophy, and Theology together into a story for you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:18:11-07:00","id":995737,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> You love Character development posts ?! Oh boy. You triggered something there xD<br /> Will be writing a longer post about Mark 5's interaction with his genitor Mudbreaker, the first months alone, the moment of him fullfilling his role etc. tomorrow, because I'll have a few hours time then =P<br /> <br /> I think I'd like to meet Mark 3 or Mark 7. Would be a curious experience to know you weren't even Mudbreaker's first attempt at fulfilling the milestone nor the last, meeting other abandoned &quot;siblings&quot;. Especially if they went Centimanus and/or turned against Mudbreaker: who to side with? Decisions, decisions... =D<br /> <br /> re Quashmallim, Principle and Divine Fire: &quot;Quashmallim are confusing, and their 'advice' only clear when everything is said an' done. They're hardly helpful. But at least you can tell you are either on the right track or very much off the track if you deal with 'em. The Divine Fire is creation itself, chaotically creating without reason or worth. By giving it reason, we can use it to make something of worth: a soul. The Principle is the Divine Fire's Will, a god of creation but without the patience needed to properly finish a job - that's why we're all half-made things.&quot;<br /> Once, in the wilderness, Mark 5 met a Quashmallim, a woman covered with frost despite the warmth, her blue eyes fixated on his chest. She was just standing there - motionless. Mark 5 had no idea what that was supposed to mean. He tried talking, but to no avail. However, when he looked around, she had moved, standing further away. He followed, but anytime he lost sight of her for even a split second, she was further away. He ran through the forest, until finally, he could not see her anymore. Instead, there was a city infront of him. An extended hand would've been a more understandable sign.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> Awesome! More players! Also, both choices seem nice and a fine addition^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:53:29-07:00","id":996053,"title":"","content":"All very good stuff. Getting a lot of ideas of where to run with the plot now. Is there anything else that my already-established players want to add about their characters, their beliefs about the setting, or things the players want to explore with the story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:09:25-07:00","id":996108,"title":"","content":"An abandoned military base is a good place to camp: people usually stay away, there is a lot of space and abandoned equipment (the soldiers would've said 'junk', but if you know what you're doing, it was good working material) and you have at least one working roof above your head. This is where Mark 5 opened his eyes for the very first time.<br /> His genitor had worked carefully, making sure to have a resilient, strong body, and it showed: Mark 5 was durable from the beginning and grew even more so with Mudbreaker's teachings. At stern teacher, she didn't pull punches, nor did she slow down when her progeny could hardly keep up. They exchanged few words; in fact, despite only having met a couple of humans within a few months, Mark 5 had exchanged more words with humans than his genitor. Then, one night, he woke up, and Mudbreaker was gone. Thinking this was another exercise, he started searching for her, but when he finally found traces, they'd gone cold hours ago.<br /> He'd never catch up. She had abandoned him.<br /> Mark 5 did not roar his rage out into the night. Instead, he carved a figure of wood, it's small, curvy figure a crude semblance of Mudbreaker's own - then, he smashed it. He did so again, 57 times (he liked counting).<br /> Inhabiting the base soon started to manifest a Wasteland, and his occasional contact with humans proved fruitless: he had hoped to make them like him by helping with cutting woods and similar tasks, but apparently some woods shouldn't be cut, and cutting too much wood made them angry because it made them look lazy and so on. It didn't take long for the first attacks, but Mark 5 weathered them. When the first Molotov hit his hut, though, he knew it was time to leave.<br /> He started moving and did not stop until the sun had set 3 times.For a short time, he lived in the woods, lost as he was. Then, he met the frozen Quashmallim.<br /> She lead him to a city. He took it to mean this was where he was going to live, now. At first, he simply wandered the city as a beggar, thinking about his life.<br /> Mudbreaker had cared for him, but she always seemed distant, disappointed. It was only later, when he learned to understand the pilgrimage that Mark 5 realized that making him had not given Mudbreaker what she had hoped for.<br /> Angry about how he was forced to flee, he decided to pick up where Mudbreaker had left him: forging a strong body, to weather the Pilgramage - and to make a nice home for his future soul. He picked up running again. He liked the sort-of-companionship you could enjoy by running the same route as others. Once, a car hit him, the owner panicked, people screamed, but when the driver was on his phone to call for help, Mark 5 managed to get up and get out. He knew then how much more abuse than humans he could take. He had to change his running route then, which was just as well: Disquiet was sure to set in sooner or later if he kept running the same ways. He climbed and even entered a gym (paid in cash) to get to lift weights (it looked so fascinating). However, the breakthrough took place elsewhere. He remembered how he was to sit motionless in the cold rain, and repeated that atop the buildings. There, he saw a small group of people, jumping from building to building. He followed. They saw him, ran faster, took ever increasing risks, and at one point, Mark 5 lost balance and plummeted to what could have been his (first) death. He pulled through, with a generous helping of electricity and blowing out a lot of Pyros to strengthen himself against the impact. He started running at the top of things more often, jumping over chasms, climbing up walls and water pipes, pulling himself up when he nearly failed a jump. He grew nimble and manoeuvrable. Then, one day, he saw the people, and took pursuit again. This time, he unfailingly gained: every time they jumped, he jumped a bit further, everytime they suddenly changed direction, he had already taken up the new direction. They dreaded the moment when he would reach them. He did... and overtook them, leaving them behind. A small band of perplexed thieves to his back, Mark 5 basked in the feeling of having overcome a tremendous challenge. There, he realized it had been his choices to train, to build himself up that enabled him to achieve this. He had endured what the world threw at him, and when he had been bested, he had grown to overcome it. He was no failure - he could CHANGE. The surge of hope near gave him wings as Mark 5 took the first step forward on his Pilgramage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unsure how you mean beliefs about the setting, could you give an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:24:54-07:00","id":996413,"title":"","content":"All good stuff. I meant in terms of what they think is out there, what weirdness they think might be real, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> When do you guys want to start the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:01:39-07:00","id":996431,"title":"","content":"Hey all, <br /> <br /> Still working out the character idea. Finally decided on Lineage though. Definitely going Frankenstien. As for the character, I think a cool idea to explore would be how more than anything else the Promethean feels like their body isn't their own. Frankenstiens are perfect for this, plus it fits the general theme of self discovery and self mastery. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T22:27:18-07:00","id":996457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=996413#post996413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All good stuff. I meant in terms of what they think is out there, what weirdness they think might be real, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> When do you guys want to start the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that Earth has a few dots in Occult and the Library (Occult) merit in the form of a bunch of handwritten journals and audio/video recordings Dead Girl made about the inexplicable weirdness they've seen on the road, because that sounds flavorful and cool. She's not really a deep thinker, but she's seen some things- &quot;a building that eats people, I've seen something like this before.&quot; Her general view is that human science and rationality isn't adequate to explain the world they live in, and the unnatural is usually ugly and violent and harmful and outsider, and represents a failure of order on some level. Some things that would definitely surprise her: organized and complex supernatural phenomena. Things that appear unnatural, but actually have a rational (if strange) explanation. Human-like societies of multiple intelligent supernatural beings parallel to human civilization, not just rogue bestial vampires and weird loners with a ghost inside them. Supernatural things that are beautiful in some way.<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with Unknown Armies at all, I love that game's take on the unnatural and the unexplained. There's a lot of stuff that's just <i>there</i>, and doesn't really have a good overarching explanation or place in an ordered cosmology, but it <i>does </i>have desperate obsessive cults and cabals fighting to control the magical exhaust it happens to produce. Even for Promethean, I always liked how their whole deal and the Principle and the Divine Fire is sort of orthogonal to the other supernaturals. The Created just kind of...are what they are, and they have this strange connection to a cosmic force and its angels, but no one really has all the puzzle pieces. It's not like Mage where a starting character can just go talk to their boss who thinks she has a pretty good idea of what's going on cosmologically.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to start whenever characters are in and you're ready. This weekend, maybe?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> That would be a good hook! Especially for a Frankenstein where their body isn't really any one person's. It would be a good excuse to get Residual Memory, maybe. Any ideas on Refinement? Plumbum might be a good way to start learning what this weirdo patchwork body is and can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-01-2016, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T02:51:22-07:00","id":996508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=996413#post996413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All good stuff. I meant in terms of what they think is out there, what weirdness they think might be real, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> When do you guys want to start the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>This weekend, like Caladriu proposed, seems like a good time if we all get ready by then =)<br /> <br /> In that case, Mark 5 knows there is more out there than Prometheans, of which he has met rather few, due to once meeting a vampire. The situation was hostile, since the vampire was feeding right then and there, and Mark 5 had only just begun his Batman-esque lifestyle. Of course, he confronted the &quot;monster&quot;, curious as to what it is. The Kindred, seeking to prevent a Masquerade breach, attacked. By the time he realized Mark 5 was not human, it was too late: The Golem wouldn't listen to his words anymore. They fought, and the vampire perished when the fight made it impossible for him to flee the coming dawn- subsequently, Mark 5 knows there are non-humans out there who prey on the living, and his status quo is they are all evil as they prey on mankind.<br /> I'm all for strange weirdness not fitting into boxes =D<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> sounds great! =D Plumbum indeed sounds like a good starting point for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:30:12-07:00","id":996553,"title":"","content":"Weekend sounds good to me. I'm having a <i>pretty </i>good idea of where to start, especially when it comes to the local supernatural goings-on, and I'm thinking we start in the present and move forwards. I think we're going to have some fun exploring these characters and seeing where the chips fall. In terms of Merits, pick what's good for your characters, don't worry too much about the fluff. Residual Memory could also be Azothic Memory leaking through, Good Brain could be the Divine Fire pushing you to excellence, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> that sounds like a good character with a lot of powerful pathos behind it; Promethean is sort of purpose-built for adventures of self-discovery, so I can't think of a better game to have that sort of storyline occur. I third the recommendation for your character starting on Plumbum, it's specifically about coming to terms with what you are and who you are. Any thoughts as to the first Role you completed and the Alembics you'll have?<br /> <br /> As a general note to all my players, remain aware of your Refinement Condition! It's an easy source of Beats and can be a great source of power. Plumbum, in particular, is easy to make into an extremely useful tool, since you can convert Bashing damage into Pyros. Here's the dice roller site I mentioned: <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller\" target=\"_blank\">http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller</a><br /> <br /> Also, just a few final considerations. Would everyone be alright with using Social Maneuvering? Both on NPCs and, potentially, with NPCs on PCs? And secondly, I'm thinking of a way to adapt the Torches and Pitchforks rules from the Hurt Locker spoilers. Basically, whenever you cause Disquiet, I add the Stage of Disquiet to a dice pool penalized by your Pilgrimage rating. Disquiet ratings go up, dice pool goes up. Success on the Disquiet pool mean the group, collectively, gains the Watched Condition or something similar, to be upgraded to Hunted on a Resolution. Exceptional Success on the Disquiet pool means a jump straight to Hunted.<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that, for quite a while, it is very unlikely that you'll be causing Disquiet in any truly noticeable fashion. You'll be rolling one die against an average of four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:29:30-07:00","id":996574,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with Social Maneuvering going both ways, and don't see a problem with the Disquiet mod.<br /> About char sheets: is sending you a pdf fine? would be easier then typing the whole thing in text since I already have one more or less done^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:47:49-07:00","id":996585,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sounds good. You can leave the character sheet on the dice roller pretty much blank, it just needs to exist so you can use the roller and I can keep track of who is doing what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:24:10-07:00","id":996805,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with Social Maneuvering being used on PCs! That would add some good drama and mechanical weight to dealing with storyteller characters who want something from us.<br /> <br /> I'm open to trying out the Torches and Pitchforks rules as you describe, although I think there's a lot of overlap between what they do mechanically and what Disquiet already does. They would be good for creating a more generalized threat at lower Disquiet levels that isn't limited to people we've Disquieted personally though.<br /> <br /> Here's my sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4imJdQ54PGfdnhzbm5Hc2dKbDA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Earth</a><br /> <br /> I spent 5 Merit dots on Azoth 2, 4 Vitriol on Azoth 3, 2 Vitriol on the Pandoran Dread Power Briareus' Prowess (taking Strength from 2 to 4), and 4 Experiences on Area of Expertise, Interdisciplinary Specialty, Efficient Conductor, and Brute Force. Is that all kosher?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:24:14-07:00","id":996996,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I'll just have to keep track of Disquiet as it comes up, which is a little easier to handle in PbP than in tabletop. Earth is looking great! It's a good spread of Merits and the addition of Dread Powers from Earth's past as Earth-Dies-Screaming is a nice touch, especially with the description of what Earth looks like with the Flux scarring.<br /> <br /> What do her Disfigurements look like? Lots of pathos in this character. And I'm pleasantly surprised that you're depicting her as a Native American individual, since it means I can dig out some of the truly ugly stuff that runs through Winnipeg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:36:16-07:00","id":997019,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to try out the torches and pitchforks, I just don't know how they'd ultimately interact with Disquieted conditions in actual play. I'm on board if you want to use them, you're the ST!<br /> <br /> I was always imagining Earth being Native, the one thing I'd add though is that I don't mean for it to be a misery tourism thing. I do think it would be interesting to find out in play how and to what degree she ID's with other Native and First Nations people, given that she's literally inhabiting a stolen body and hasn't been part of any human community. On the other hand, she's not really anything else. I feel like Promethean is like Demon in that its protagonists don't necessarily have to have a concrete relationship to the race or gender or etc of their bodies as humans see them.<br /> <br /> Disfigurements: Her hair is muddy and matted, she's got furrows and pebbles embedded in her, her nails are craggy and dirty- she looks like she got shot point blank with buckshot, buried in a shallow grave, and clawed her way out. And thanks to her Flux scars, her skin has streaks of different colors and she's tongue-tied and her right hand looks like some kinda flabby devil claw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:40:27-07:00","id":997204,"title":"","content":"So....<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_FPs8g35aBYWXpudl9WT1BPejQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">I hope this works, never used Google drive before.</a><br /> <br /> I spent 4 vitriolic xp on Azoth 2, 4 xp on Dext 3 and 2 xp on Stealth 2. Also corrected Unbowed to Unconquered (Unbowed is kinda fixed on resisting mental/social stress, which would be weird for Mark 5, imo). Hope everything is okay^^&quot;<br /> <br /> @Disfigurements: there are larger stones stuck in Mark 5's skin (the 'scabs'), and he is covered completely by dust. The skin on his fingers is torn open, his eyes are glassy and dark. There is a big wound on the Torso, as if cut with a machette or something similarly large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:46:04-07:00","id":997236,"title":"","content":"I got the file- all is good <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>. Just one final question regarding your character; what is Mark 5's inscription? All Tammuz are marked in some way, so what's Mark's unique variation on that particular theme?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I have no intention to make the game misery tourism- it's a horror game, but I like my Promethean to have a heavy dose of hope. I'm more excited at the opportunity for an easy Disquiet vector that also allows for some real world issues to be broached.<br /> <br /> Anyways, seeing as things are more or less set to go, I think I'll post the OOC and IC threads at some point tomorrow or Friday. I know I can handle at least two posts a day, but we can increase (or lower) that frequency as need be. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> how's your character coming along?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:02:58-07:00","id":997246,"title":"","content":"I really like that, even by &quot;cheating&quot; with Flux, Earth just isn't as strong as Mark 5 and doesn't have as many Physical dots. On the surface, he's exactly the kind of Tammuz her creator wanted. I might swap Brute Force for Residual Memory just to differentiate them a little more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:23:54-07:00","id":997260,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> I hadn't noticed, that's actually pretty cool! A dash of smoldering animosity due to envy added to their relationship due to that, perchance? =D<br /> Then again, Mark's 'cheating' with Ferrum, too =P<br /> I actually like you having Brute Force, too. The vengeful former-demon crushing people with pure force (makes me think of some sort of Darth Vader), and the aspiring hero being just as bad due to not &quot;getting it&quot; (...early Arrow?). Nice symbolism, anywho, imo.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> Totally forgot about that; it's a single word (Survivor), brandmarked into his chest, above his heart.<br /> 2 posts a day is fine by me, sounds like a decent pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:21:44-07:00","id":997400,"title":"","content":"Hey all, still working out the sheet itself, some RL stuff has been delaying my progress but with some luck I should have it done by tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:30:00-07:00","id":997590,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've run into a bit more of a snag than I bargained for. My laptop has officially died, and without it my only means of reading the PtC 2E PDF I have are gone with it since my phone isn't powerful enough to read it from Dropbox without crash-lagging. I'll see what I can do to fix this problem, but for now you guys should just go on without me. My technical troubles shouldn't keep you all from gaming, and with any luck I might still be able to salvage my laptop and get it up and running again soon and just join the game then. <br /> <br /> Just want to say thanks for letting me have the chance to play in a Promethean Chronicle though, it's been a game I've been wanting to explore for a while and with any luck I still might be able too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-03-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T02:11:37-07:00","id":997615,"title":"","content":"Aww, that sucks! Hope you'll be able to join soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:32:09-07:00","id":997913,"title":"","content":"That sucks, sorry Dusksage. I hope you're able to join at some point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:43:12-07:00","id":997917,"title":"","content":"Good luck, Dusksage! <br /> <br /> Now having the opportunity to partake in PbP games, part of me wants to jump in. But I'm not entirely sure if there's any etiquette or rules of thumb on when to join other games: six months, a year? Not that I'm not enjoying the hell out of my current Mage game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:48:29-07:00","id":997921,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> ayyyyyy<br /> <br /> I don't think there's any etiquette- this forum isn't really active enough to have a rule, it's actually pretty miraculous that Supernal Suburbia has been going strong for so long. Jump on in!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:46:21-07:00","id":997983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> I'm sorry that your laptop has failed you. Hopefully you'll be able to join us at a later date, we'd be happy to have you!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> Jump right on in! We'd be happy to have you! Throw a character together and come and join us, the Pilgrimage is a lonely road- a fellow traveler is a sight for sore eyes.<br /> <br /> That said, I think I've got a title for the game: Muddy Waters. That or &quot;Clear as Mud&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:03:57-07:00","id":997988,"title":"","content":"&quot;MUDSPORT&quot;<br /> &quot;MUD AND STEEL&quot;<br /> &quot;THRONE OF MUD&quot;<br /> &quot;MUD IN THE WATER&quot;<br /> &quot;FIRST MUD&quot;<br /> &quot;PROMETHEAN: THE CREATED: MUDLINES&quot;<br /> <br /> edit: here's some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/997407-npc-sunny-and-the-kid\">#content</a> i made if it gives our ST any ideas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-03-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:32:23-07:00","id":998266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/994549-starting-a-promethean-game?p=997917#post997917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck, Dusksage!<br /> <br /> Now having the opportunity to partake in PbP games, part of me wants to jump in. But I'm not entirely sure if there's any etiquette or rules of thumb on when to join other games: six months, a year? Not that I'm not enjoying the hell out of my current Mage game!</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome and glad to have you! =D<br /> <br /> Muddy Waters sounds nice. Either that or &quot;Promethean: the Created - Mudlines&quot; xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:42:28-07:00","id":998307,"title":"","content":"Here's the OOC thread guys! <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...e-muddy-waters<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">EDIT: Here's the IC thread! </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998318-ic-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters</span></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-04-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:21:30-08:00","id":1009764,"title":"","content":"Hey how's it going? I started a Facebook group for White Wolf game play media and subject matter media but we also allow people who are trying to run a game post looking for players too. The only thing we ask is the following;<br /> <br /> 1)Be specific on the game type, and theme of the game<br /> 2)Be specific on what you will allow and not allow<br /> 3)The means in which you plan to run the game, and when.<br /> 4)The more details the better.<br /> <br /> Hope to see you there!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/rsrc.php/y8/r/dF5SId3UHWd.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\"> Log into Facebook </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:31:04-08:00","id":1023892,"title":"","content":"*runs skidding into the room*<br /> <br /> I found a way to access my 2nd Edition Copy of Promethean: the Created 2nd Edition! *pant* I can...*pant*...join the game now if you'll all still have me...*pant*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:17:43-08:00","id":1024862,"title":"","content":"My Azothic Memory is tingling...I must...show my current character concept...<br /> <br /> &gt; Name: Regret<br /> &gt; Concept: Seeker of Identity<br /> &gt; Lineage: Frankenstein<br /> &gt; Refinement: Plumbum<br /> ~ Role: Pilgrim<br /> &gt; Elpis: Sorrow<br /> &gt; Torment: Merciless<br /> &gt; Mental Attributes: Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 2<br /> &gt; Physical Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> &gt; Social Attributes: Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 2<br /> &gt; Mental Skills: Crafts 2, Investigation 1, Science 1<br /> &gt; Physical Skills: Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms (Rifles) 2, Larceny 1, Survival (Wilderness Training) 1, Weaponry 2<br /> &gt; Social Skills: Empathy (Suffering) 2, Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 1<br /> &gt; Merits: Ambidextrous (3), Danger Sense (2), Residual Memory - Expression/Larceny/Science (3), Safe Place - The Far Place (2)<br /> &gt; Bestowments: Titan's Strength<br /> &gt; Transmutations<br /> ~ Disquietism: Externalize<br /> ~ Saturninus: Plumb the Fathoms<br /> &gt; Health: 8 = 00000000<br /> &gt; Willpower: 4 = ++++<br /> &gt; Size: 5<br /> &gt; Speed: 10<br /> &gt; Initiative: 4<br /> &gt; Defense: 4<br /> &gt; Pilgrimage: 1<br /> &gt; Azoth: 1<br /> &gt; Pyros: 5/10<br /> &gt; Aspirations<br /> ~ Meet the other PCs<br /> ~ Utilize the Safe Place Merit<br /> ~ Discover an Athanor<br /> &gt; Conditions<br /> ~ Introspective (Refinement)<br /> ~ ?<br /> ~ ?<br /> &gt; Exp: 0<br /> &gt; Vitriol Exp: 0<br /> &gt;Synopsis: Regret was created by a Promethean who always found their own body to be sub par. They were created out of what their Genitor thought was perfect specimens, and in the end they found their body too frail and unprepared for the harshness of the Pilgrimage. So, when they created Regret they made him out of what they thought were the perfect specimens: soldiers. Piece by piece they built their creation out of soldiers, thinking there was no finer material that could handle the rigors of the Pilgrimage. But they didn't understand the horrors of warfare, and so Regret is haunted by the stolen lives that comprise his body. But there is one blessing that came from his creation, Sorrow. The fragments of his being remember the depth of human suffering, even if just instinctively. This has allowed Regret to look upon his own actions through the lens of pointless folly and necessary sacrifice. When one action slides to far towards folly he knows he hasn't acted right, and this guides his morality as he slowly marches towards the New Dawn. His greatest hindrance is how easy it is for him and his body to kill. Violence is second nature, and it almost always after the fact that Regret's Elpis reminds him of why he seeks humanity, and why he shouldn't bring war to the human world. <br /> <br /> <br /> Pilgrimage Questions<br /> <br /> Q: What Sort of Human Do You Want to Be?<br /> A: A peacemaker, someone who can resolve conflict without violence. Someone who can stem human suffering and lead humans away from war.<br /> <br /> Q: How Have Humans Taught You To Fear and Hate?<br /> A: Humans are always so quick to point blade and gun at anything they believe dangerous. Human ignorance and pride are the mother an father of suffering. If only is wasn't so easy to understand why they fear for their lives. <br /> <br /> Q: How Did You Split With Your Creator?<br /> A: They didn't understand why I hated my body, they built it so they could protect me from their own fears but failed to realize I wasn't them. If only they knew what it's like to have every inch of their being crying out to go home...<br /> <br /> Q: What Keeps You on the Pilgrimage?<br /> A: They were never able to go home, so I will bring them all a second chance at life. At the human kindness they were denied at the hour of their deaths.<br /> <br /> Q: What Would You Give Up to Become Human?<br /> A: Conventional Morality, after all it is a lie. There is no good and evil, there is only you and the one who has the gun. Every other decision is purely based on personal ignorance and pride. We're all proof of that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Done 12-31-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T21:11:21-08:00","id":1024994,"title":"","content":"Hop over to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/998305-ooc-promethean-the-created-2e-muddy-waters/page11\">OOC thread</a> and introduce yourself. We'd be happy to have you. Your character starts with a completed Role and 10XP, divided between Vitriol and Experiences however you'd like. All I need is for you to describe the Milestone for completing the Role and what Regret learned from it. Are there any particular Refinements you'd like your character to pursue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:06:58-08:00","id":1025250,"title":"","content":"Hi, so I just got the copy of the 2e corebook and I'm looking to join once I get a bit of the book under my belt. What do I need to join?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}